                <pb facs="0448" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3335: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Paraguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Horn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-09-29T10:00:00-04:00">September 29, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12 noon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93. Department’s telegram No. 27, September 27, 6 p.m.<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d320-f1"/> At noon today I conveyed the message as desired to the
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs. He expressed his Government’s appreciation of the
                    friendly interest manifested by the United States and promised a more responsive
                    answer after the message had been duly considered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
